    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d142-a2">

                <pb facs="0378" n="294" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg294"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in note of August 31,
                    1886.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Flores to Mr. Kelly, contractor of the Southern
                        Railroad, Ecuador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Ecuador</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">New
                            York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1886-06-26"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">June</hi> 26, 1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Kelly</hi>: Will you be so good as to
                    answer mo the following questions, authorizing me to make use of your
                    answers?</p>
                <list>
                    <label>(1)</label>
                    <item>Which is your nationality?</item>
                    <label>(2)</label>
                    <item>When you left Ecuador recently, did you have to provide yourself with a
                        passport?</item>
                    <label>(3)</label>
                    <item>Do you consider that you relinquish your nationality by receiving a
                        passport?</item>
                </list>
                <p>Very sincerely, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed>A. FLORES.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
